  "name": "Deutsche Börse",
  "note": "2010-2024 sourced from exchange_calendars only (backfill; not independently verified): 104 closures and 15 early closes (14:00 on the last trading day of each year, exchange_calendars' value). 2025-2026: exchange_calendars + exchange_publications. 2027-2029: the same non-trading days, with the last-trading-day early closes predicted (4d.1). Checked 2026-11-20 (4c8). Non-trading days: Deutsche Börse's trading calendar (https://cashmarket.deutsche-boerse.com/cash-en/trading/trading-calendar-and-trading-hours) lists Xetra non-trading days for 2026-2032; the registry matches 2026, 2027, 2028 and 2029 exactly (Ascension Day, Whit Monday and Corpus Christi are trading days). Close (ADR 0013): Deutsche Börse's Xetra trading parameters as of 1 December 2025 (https://cashmarket.deutsche-boerse.com/resource/blob/250890/43c50e657b0ff5fb58132fbf6e063517/data/trading-parameters-xetra.pdf) give the closing auction call at 17:30 and the closing auction price at 17:35, and the auction schedule (https://cashmarket.deutsche-boerse.com/cash-en/trading/Xetra/continuous-trading-with-auctions/auctionschedule) says auctions have a random end and the times stated are the earliest end times. regular_hours.close is therefore 17:35 (was 17:30, the end of continuous trading; exchange_calendars has 17:30). regular_hours is two entries with the same 09:00-17:35, 2010-01-01 (marked unconfirmed: no earlier Deutsche Börse schedule was read) and 2025-12-01 (the parameter sheet's date). The closing auction entry in sessions, post_market and extended_hours.after_hours move to 17:35; the Extended Xetra Retail Service (late trading to 22:00 since 2025-12-01) is not modelled here. Early closes: the last trading day of the year is shortened. Deutsche Börse's announcement for 30 December 2025 (https://www.cashmarket.deutsche-boerse.com/resource/blob/4580834/14d7f01321cb1d949020067efd2ee174/data/Final%20trading%20session%202025.pdf) gives the Xetra closing auction call from 2.00 p.m. with earliest price determination at 2.05 p.m. and trade-at-close until 2.15 p.m., so 2025-12-30 is an early close at 14:05 (ADR 0013). For 30 December 2026 Deutsche Börse's homepage (https://cashmarket.deutsche-boerse.com/cash-de/) announces a last trading day with an early close (circular 050/2026), but the time was not read: 14:05 is used, following 2025, and the 2025-2026 span marks 2026-12-30 unconfirmed with recheck_date 2026-12-15. 2027-12-30, 2028-12-29 and 2029-12-28 (the last trading days) are predicted early closes at 14:05: the trading-calendar page (read 2026-11-21) says only 'On December 30, 2026, deviating trading hours may apply', the hours coming by circular each year. The 2010-2024 backfill keeps exchange_calendars' 14:00 (end of continuous trading), a convention difference from ADR 0013. The Xetra fetcher cannot reach deutsche-boerse.com from this sandbox; the sources were read by hand.",
